{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport galaxy_cli, inspect, os\nprint(galaxy_cli.__file__)\nprint(dir(galaxy_cli)[:100])\nPY\npython3 -m galaxy_cli --help 2>&1 | head -100 || true\"","aggregated_output":"/opt/agent-venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/galaxy_cli/__init__.py\n['PackageNotFoundError', '__builtins__', '__cached__', '__doc__', '__file__', '__loader__', '__name__', '__package__', '__path__', '__spec__', '__version__', 'version']\nUsage: galaxy-cli [OPTIONS] [COMMAND] [ARGS]...\n\n  CLI harness for Galaxy bioinformatics platform.\n\n  Connect to a running Galaxy server and manage histories, datasets, tools,\n  workflows, and jobs from the command line.\n\n  Output mode:\n    Compact JSON is the default.\n    Use --human for human-readable terminal output.\n\n  Quick start (typical tool task):\n    source .env                      # set GALAXY_URL + GALAXY_API_KEY\n    galaxy-cli history create \"my run\"\n    galaxy-cli dataset upload data.tsv --history-id HID\n    galaxy-cli tool search \"cut columns\"\n    galaxy-cli tool show Cut1\n    galaxy-cli tool run Cut1 --history-id HID -i input=DSID --wait\n    galaxy-cli dataset show OUTPUT_ID\n\n  Quick start (workflow task):\n    galaxy-cli workflow import workflow.ga\n    galaxy-cli workflow show WF_ID\n    galaxy-cli workflow run WF_ID --history-id HID -i 0=DSID --wait\n\nOptions:\n  --url TEXT         Galaxy server URL\n  --api-key TEXT     Galaxy API key\n  --profile TEXT     Use a named profile from ~/.galaxy-cli/config.json for\n                     this command\n  --history-id TEXT  Override current history ID\n  --json / --human   JSON output (default) or human-readable output\n  --version          Show the version and exit.\n  --help             Show this message and exit.\n\nCommands:\n  collection  Manage dataset collections.\n  config      Manage Galaxy server connection settings.\n  dataset     Manage datasets in